{%- comment -%}
  The "See how it works" modal for the free AI travel planner.

  The gift row it explains is drawn by the Bundlex app, so there is no block to add
  this to and no markup we can edit. assets/voltairs-planner-modal.js finds that row
  by its title text and appends the trigger, then re-appends it whenever the app
  re-renders. gift_labels below is what it matches on, so if the offer's wording ever
  changes in Bundlex, change it here too or the link quietly stops appearing.

  All the copy lives in this file. The two demo answers on the third slide are typed
  out by the script, which reads them straight from the markup, so they stay readable
  if the script never runs.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign gift_labels = 'Secret AI Travel Upgrade, AI Travel Upgrade, Smart Travel Planner, AI Travel Planner' | split: ','
  assign link_label = 'See how it works'
  assign gpt_logo = 'ChatGPT-Logo.png' | file_url

  comment
    Shown under the file on the first slide. It has to match the name of the PDF the
    shopper actually downloads, or the modal is describing a different file.
  endcomment
  assign planner_file_name = 'AI-Travel-Planner.pdf'
-%}

{%- if request.page_type == 'product' -%}
  {{ 'voltairs-planner-modal.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

  <script type="application/json" id="voltairs-planner-modal-config">
    {
      "labels": {{ gift_labels | json }},
      "linkLabel": {{ link_label | json }}
    }
  </script>

  <dialog class="vpm" id="vpm-dialog" aria-label="How the AI travel planner works">
    <div class="vpm-sheet">
      <header class="vpm-head">
        <button class="vpm-close" type="button" data-vpm-close aria-label="Close">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M1 1l12 12M13 1L1 13" />
          </svg>
        </button>
      </header>

      <div class="vpm-track" data-vpm-track>
        {%- comment -%} 1. What is this {%- endcomment -%}
        <section class="vpm-slide" data-vpm-slide aria-label="What is this">
          <h3 class="vpm-slide-title">What is this?</h3>

          {%- comment -%}
            One scene, played out: the prompt is typed, the cursor attaches the
            planner, hits send, and everything the file carries pours into ChatGPT,
            whose mark then picks up an orbit and a plane.

            Steps run in document order, which is why the <i> cues sit between the
            things they act on, and why the attachment chip is written after the input
            row and lifted above it with `order`. The cues are invisible: every
            [data-vpm-step] starts out display:none. The whole figure is decorative,
            so it is hidden from assistive tech and the paragraph under it says the
            same thing in words.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <figure class="vpm-scene" aria-hidden="true" data-vpm-seq data-vpm-speed="18" data-vpm-loop="2600" data-phase="idle">
            <div class="vpm-chat">
              <div class="vpm-chat-row">
                <span class="vpm-chat-btn" data-vpm-target="attach">
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                    <path d="M20 11.5l-8.4 8.4a4.6 4.6 0 0 1-6.5-6.5l8.4-8.4a3 3 0 0 1 4.3 4.3l-8.4 8.4a1.5 1.5 0 0 1-2.2-2.2l7.8-7.8" />
                  </svg>
                </span>
                <p class="vpm-chat-text"><span class="vpm-chat-say" data-vpm-step="type">Plan my trip from NY to Paris</span></p>
                <span class="vpm-chat-btn vpm-chat-send" data-vpm-target="send">
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                    <path d="M12 19V5" />
                    <path d="M6 11l6-6 6 6" />
                  </svg>
                </span>
              </div>

              <i data-vpm-step="move" data-vpm-to="attach"></i>
              <i data-vpm-step="click" data-vpm-to="attach"></i>

              <span class="vpm-chat-file" data-vpm-step="show">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6">
                  <path d="M14 3H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z" />
                  <path d="M14 3v5h5" />
                </svg>
                {{ planner_file_name }}
                <em>80+ pages</em>
              </span>

              <i data-vpm-step="move" data-vpm-to="send"></i>
              <i data-vpm-step="click" data-vpm-to="send"></i>

              {%- comment -%}
                Two phases: everything the file carries pours in, and only once it
                has all landed does the mark turn into the travel one.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                The hold has to outlast the pour or the logo turns while badges are
                still in the air. 25 badges, 0.42s apart, 1.5s each: see vpm-fall.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <i data-vpm-step="state" data-vpm-state="sent" data-vpm-hold="12400"></i>
              <i data-vpm-step="state" data-vpm-state="ready" data-vpm-hold="2600"></i>

              <span class="vpm-cursor" data-vpm-cursor>
                <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor">
                  <path d="M1 1l5.2 13 2.1-5.3L13.6 6.6z" />
                </svg>
              </span>
            </div>

            <div class="vpm-lane">
              <b style="--i: 0; --x: 4%">Flight search</b>
              <b style="--i: 1; --x: 46%">Cheaper dates</b>
              <b style="--i: 2; --x: 24%">Airport swaps</b>
              <b style="--i: 3; --x: 58%">Child fares</b>
              <b style="--i: 4; --x: 12%">Baggage costs</b>
              <b style="--i: 5; --x: 38%">Layover safety</b>
              <b style="--i: 6; --x: 2%">Self-transfer risk</b>
              <b style="--i: 7; --x: 50%">Hotel zones</b>
              <b style="--i: 8; --x: 28%">Hidden hotel fees</b>
              <b style="--i: 9; --x: 16%">Free cancellation</b>
              <b style="--i: 10; --x: 20%">Airport transfer</b>
              <b style="--i: 11; --x: 8%">Car rental traps</b>
              <b style="--i: 12; --x: 34%">Parking + tolls</b>
              <b style="--i: 13; --x: 54%">City passes</b>
              <b style="--i: 14; --x: 20%">Ticket discounts</b>
              <b style="--i: 15; --x: 40%">Restaurant picks</b>
              <b style="--i: 16; --x: 6%">Allergy + halal</b>
              <b style="--i: 17; --x: 30%">Tripadvisor scan</b>
              <b style="--i: 18; --x: 52%">Reddit scan</b>
              <b style="--i: 19; --x: 14%">Weather windows</b>
              <b style="--i: 20; --x: 36%">Strikes + closures</b>
              <b style="--i: 21; --x: 60%">Visa + entry</b>
              <b style="--i: 22; --x: 10%">eSIM + card fees</b>
              <b style="--i: 23; --x: 26%">Packing plan</b>
              <b style="--i: 24; --x: 42%">True trip cost</b>
            </div>

            {%- comment -%}
              The mark starts as the plain ChatGPT logo the store already has in
              Files. The orbit and the plane are drawn here rather than loaded as a
              second logo, so the plain mark turns into the travel one on screen
              instead of swapping between two static images.

              The ring is two arcs: the long one draws itself, the short one dashes
              in behind the plane. pathLength normalises both to 100 units so the
              dash maths does not depend on the radius.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="vpm-ai">
              <span class="vpm-ai-mark">
                {%- if gpt_logo != blank -%}
                  <img src="{{ gpt_logo }}" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy">
                {%- else -%}
                  <svg class="vpm-ai-fallback" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round">
                    <path d="M20 15a3 3 0 0 1-3 3H8l-4 3V6a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h10a3 3 0 0 1 3 3z" />
                  </svg>
                {%- endif -%}

                <svg class="vpm-orbit" viewBox="0 0 60 60" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round">
                  <path class="vpm-orbit-solid" pathLength="100" d="M13.3 10.1A26 26 0 1 0 52.5 43" />
                  <path class="vpm-orbit-dashes" pathLength="100" stroke-dasharray="4 6" d="M52.5 43A26 26 0 0 0 13.3 10.1" />
                </svg>

                <span class="vpm-orbiter">
                  <svg class="vpm-plane" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor">
                    <path d="M12 2c-1 0-1.6 1-1.6 2.4v4.2L3 13.2v2.3l7.4-2.2v4.3l-2.2 1.6v1.8L12 20l3.8 1v-1.8l-2.2-1.6v-4.3l7.4 2.2v-2.3l-7.4-4.6V4.4C13.6 3 13 2 12 2z" />
                  </svg>
                </span>
              </span>

              <span class="vpm-ai-label">
                <b class="vpm-ai-was">ChatGPT</b>
                <b class="vpm-ai-now">Your travel agent</b>
              </span>
            </div>
          </figure>

          <p class="vpm-sr">
            Type a trip into ChatGPT, attach {{ planner_file_name }}, and 80 or more
            pages of method go in with it: flight and date search, airport swaps,
            child fares, baggage and layover checks, hotel zones and hidden fees,
            transfers, car rental traps, city passes and ticket discounts, restaurant
            picks with allergy and halal checks, Tripadvisor and Reddit scans, weather
            windows, strikes and closures, visa and entry rules, card fees, packing,
            and the true cost of the whole trip.
          </p>

          <p class="vpm-scene-copy">Your AI reads all 80+ pages in seconds, then plans with the hacks, best practices and hidden gems inside.</p>

          <p class="vpm-foot">You do not read it. Your AI does.</p>
        </section>

        {%- comment -%}
          2. What it gets you. Cards deal in one at a time, driven by --i and the
          is-active class, so nothing moves until the slide is actually on screen.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <section class="vpm-slide" data-vpm-slide aria-label="What you get">
          <h3 class="vpm-slide-title">What you get</h3>

          <ul class="vpm-wins">
            <li class="vpm-win" style="--i: 0">
              <span class="vpm-win-ic" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <path d="M12 4v16" />
                  <path d="M15.5 8.2A3 3 0 0 0 12.8 6.5h-1.4a2.6 2.6 0 0 0-.6 5.1l2.6.7a2.6 2.6 0 0 1-.6 5.2h-1.4a3 3 0 0 1-2.7-1.7" />
                </svg>
              </span>
              <b class="vpm-win-h">Save $100+ a trip</b>
              <span class="vpm-win-p">The date, airport and fee checks that move the number.</span>
            </li>

            <li class="vpm-win" style="--i: 1">
              <span class="vpm-win-ic" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <path d="M2 12s3.6-6 10-6 10 6 10 6-3.6 6-10 6-10-6-10-6z" />
                  <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2.6" />
                </svg>
              </span>
              <b class="vpm-win-h">Hidden costs, surfaced</b>
              <span class="vpm-win-p">Baggage, resort fees, tolls, card charges. Before you book.</span>
            </li>

            <li class="vpm-win" style="--i: 2">
              <span class="vpm-win-ic" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <path d="M20 14.5a2.5 2.5 0 0 1-2.5 2.5H9l-4.5 3.5V6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 7 4h10.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 20 6.5z" />
                  <path d="M10.2 9a2 2 0 0 1 3.7 1c0 1.3-2 1.6-2 2.7" />
                  <path d="M11.9 15.2h.01" />
                </svg>
              </span>
              <b class="vpm-win-h">A planner that asks first</b>
              <span class="vpm-win-p">Budget, dates, who is coming. Then it plans around you.</span>
            </li>

            <li class="vpm-win" style="--i: 3">
              <span class="vpm-win-ic" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <path d="M6 3v7a2 2 0 0 0 4 0V3" />
                  <path d="M8 10v11" />
                  <path d="M17 3c-1.7 1.4-2.5 3.4-2.5 5.6 0 1.6.8 2.6 2.5 2.9V21" />
                </svg>
              </span>
              <b class="vpm-win-h">Food that fits you</b>
              <span class="vpm-win-p">Allergies, halal and diets checked on every recommendation.</span>
            </li>

            <li class="vpm-win" style="--i: 4">
              <span class="vpm-win-ic" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <path d="M12 3.6l2.5 5.1 5.6.8-4 4 .9 5.6-5-2.7-5 2.7.9-5.6-4-4 5.6-.8z" />
                </svg>
              </span>
              <b class="vpm-win-h">Real reviews, not ads</b>
              <span class="vpm-win-p">Tripadvisor, Reddit and Google cross-checked before it picks.</span>
            </li>

            <li class="vpm-win" style="--i: 5">
              <span class="vpm-win-ic" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <path d="M12 3l7.5 3v6c0 4.4-3.1 7.7-7.5 9-4.4-1.3-7.5-4.6-7.5-9V6z" />
                  <path d="M9 12.2l2 2 4-4.2" />
                </svg>
              </span>
              <b class="vpm-win-h">Nothing derails it</b>
              <span class="vpm-win-p">Weather, strikes, closures and entry rules checked ahead.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>

          <p class="vpm-foot" style="--i: 6">One file. Every trip you take from here.</p>
        </section>

        {%- comment -%} 3. The difference {%- endcomment -%}
        <section class="vpm-slide" data-vpm-slide aria-label="See the difference">
          <h3 class="vpm-slide-title">See the difference</h3>

          {%- comment -%}
            The demo is an illustration, so it is hidden from assistive tech and this
            line stands in for it. Streaming half-typed fragments to a screen reader
            would be worse than describing what the illustration shows.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <p class="vpm-sr">
            Asked to plan a trip to London in October, plain ChatGPT returns a generic
            day-by-day list. With the planner, it flags the October weather, asks what
            budget to target, offers travel weeks with a recommendation, and starts the
            plan with flights.
          </p>

          <div class="vpm-demo" data-vpm-demo data-stage="idle" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="vpm-cols">
              <article class="vpm-col vpm-col--plain" data-vpm-seq data-vpm-speed="60">
                <p class="vpm-col-head">
                  {%- if gpt_logo != blank -%}
                    <img src="{{ gpt_logo }}" alt="" width="16" height="16" loading="lazy">
                  {%- endif -%}
                  <span>ChatGPT</span>
                </p>
                <div class="vpm-thread">
                  <p class="vpm-said">Plan a trip to London in October</p>
                  <p class="vpm-bubble" data-vpm-step="type">Sure! Here's a 5-day London itinerary:
                    Day 1: Tower of London
                    Day 2: British Museum
                    Day 3: Camden Market
                    Let me know if you want more detail.</p>
                </div>
                <p class="vpm-cap">Generic. You still do all the work.</p>
              </article>

              <article class="vpm-col vpm-col--planner" data-vpm-seq data-vpm-speed="95">
                <p class="vpm-col-head">
                  {%- if gpt_logo != blank -%}
                    <img src="{{ gpt_logo }}" alt="" width="16" height="16" loading="lazy">
                  {%- endif -%}
                  <span>ChatGPT travel agent</span>
                </p>
                <div class="vpm-thread">
                  <p class="vpm-said">Plan a trip to London in October</p>

                  <p class="vpm-bubble" data-vpm-step="type">Nice choice. October in London is rainy but manageable, so layers matter more than an extra outfit.

                    Trip reports put a couple's October week at roughly $2,000 to $4,000 all in. What budget should I target?</p>

                  <p class="vpm-said" data-vpm-step="show">$2,000</p>

                  <p class="vpm-bubble" data-vpm-step="type">Good, that works. When are you traveling, and for how long?</p>

                  <ul class="vpm-opts" data-vpm-step="reveal">
                    <li data-vpm-pick>First week <em>Recommended: cheaper flights, better weather</em></li>
                    <li>Second week</li>
                    <li>Third week</li>
                  </ul>

                  <p class="vpm-said" data-vpm-step="show">First week, 7 days</p>

                  <p class="vpm-bubble" data-vpm-step="type">Then let's start with flights. One week is short, so it makes no sense to spend it in airports. I will also look for tickets available for resale.</p>
                </div>
                <p class="vpm-cap">Asks the right questions, then plans around your answers.</p>
              </article>
            </div>

            <div class="vpm-demo-foot">
              <p class="vpm-note">Illustrative example.</p>
              <button class="vpm-replay" type="button" data-vpm-replay>Replay</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>

      <nav class="vpm-nav" aria-label="Slides">
        <button class="vpm-arrow" type="button" data-vpm-prev aria-label="Previous">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 13 13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M8.5 1.5L3 6.5l5.5 5" />
          </svg>
        </button>
        <div class="vpm-dots">
          <button class="vpm-dot" type="button" data-vpm-dot aria-current="true" aria-label="What is this"></button>
          <button class="vpm-dot" type="button" data-vpm-dot aria-current="false" aria-label="What you get"></button>
          <button class="vpm-dot" type="button" data-vpm-dot aria-current="false" aria-label="See the difference"></button>
        </div>
        <button class="vpm-arrow" type="button" data-vpm-next aria-label="Next">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 13 13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M4.5 1.5L10 6.5l-5.5 5" />
          </svg>
        </button>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </dialog>

  <script src="{{ 'voltairs-planner-modal.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endif -%}
